    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="toc">

                <pb facs="0011" n="VII" xml:id="pgVII"/>

                <head>Contents</head>
                <list type="toc">
                    <item>
                        <ref target="#pgIII">
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Preface</hi>
                        </ref>
                    </item>
                    <item>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">General</hi>: <list>
                            <item>Activities of the Soviet Union in Eastern Europe, and Soviet
                                relations with the belligerent powers: <list>
                                    <item>
                                        <ref target="#pg1">I. Relations between Finland and the
                                            Soviet Union, and the attempts of the United States to
                                            persuade Finland not to participate in the war against
                                            the Soviet Union in association with Germany</ref>
                                    </item>
                                    <item>
                                        <ref target="#pg116">II. Wartime cooperation between Germany
                                            and the Soviet Union until the German attack of June 22,
                                            1941</ref>
                                    </item>
                                    <item>
                                        <ref target="#pg155">III. Wartime attempts of the United
                                            Kingdom and France to obtain closer relations with the
                                            Soviet Union</ref>
                                    </item>
                                </list>
                            </item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg206">Interest of the United States in the Polish
                                    Government in Exile, and in its relations with the Soviet Union,
                                    1939–1941</ref>
                            </item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg272">Interest of the United States in German and
                                    Soviet activities in the Balkan States</ref>
                            </item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg340">The Axis war against Greece</ref>
                            </item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg341">The Atlantic Conference between President
                                    Roosevelt and Prime Minister Churchill, August 9–12, 1941</ref>
                            </item>
                            <item>Neutrality policy of the United States: <list>
                                    <item>
                                        <ref target="#pg379">I. Repeal of sections 2, 3, and 6 of
                                            the Neutrality Act by law approved November 17,
                                            1941</ref>
                                    </item>
                                    <item>
                                        <ref target="#pg379">II. Measures for the maintenance of
                                            neutrality of the United States and expansion of the
                                            national defense</ref>
                                    </item>
                                    <item>
                                        <ref target="#pg381">III. Measures taken to assist British
                                            war effort in connection with neutrality policies of the
                                            United States</ref>
                                    </item>
                                </list>
                            </item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg398">Emergency measures for the repatriation of
                                    American citizens abroad with the spread of war in Europe</ref>
                            </item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg434">Cooperation with the Intergovernmental
                                    Committee on Refugees to assist persons forced to emigrate,
                                    primarily from Germany, for political or racial reasons</ref>
                            </item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg445">Allied declarations condemning German
                                    atrocities in occupied territories</ref>
                            </item>
                            <item>Measures taken by the United States to secure adequate supplies of
                                war material, food, and shipping for defense purposes: <list>
                                    <item>
                                        <ref target="#pg451">I. Seizure and requisition of German
                                            and Italian ships lying in United States ports</ref>
                                    </item>
                                    <item>
                                        <ref target="#pg485">II. Suspension of the Load Line
                                            Convention for the duration of the emergency</ref>
                                    </item>
                                    <item>
                                        <ref target="#pg492">III. Negotiations with the
                                            International Rubber Regulation Committee, through the
                                            British and Netherlands Governments, for adequate
                                            supplies of rubber</ref>
                                    </item>
                                    <pb facs="0012" n="VIII" xml:id="pgVIII"/>
                                    <item>
                                        <ref target="#pg507">IV. Interest of the United States in
                                            the renewal of the international agreement of January 5,
                                            1937, to regulate the production and export of tin</ref>
                                    </item>
                                    <item>
                                        <ref target="#pg530">V. Participation of the United States
                                            in the International Wheat Meeting at Washington, July
                                            1941–April 1942</ref>
                                    </item>
                                </list>
                            </item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg557">Protests of foreign governments against certain
                                    provisions of the Selective Training and Service Act of 1940,
                                    resulting in amendment of the Act</ref>
                            </item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg573">Arrangements by the United States for the
                                    establishment of military air bases on Pacific Islands for route
                                    from Hawaii to the Philippines</ref>
                            </item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg585">Status of intergovernmental debts owed the
                                    United States by reason of the First World War</ref>
                            </item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg587">Declarations of state of war between the Axis
                                    countries and the United States</ref>
                            </item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg593">Protection of American interests in enemy
                                    countries by the Swiss Government</ref>
                            </item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg594">Creation in the Department of State of the
                                    Advisory Committee on Postwar Foreign Policy</ref>
                            </item>
                        </list>
                    </item>
                    <item>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Union of Soviet Socialist Republics</hi>: <list>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg597">Reports on developments of significance
                                    concerning Soviet relations with other countries, especially
                                    with the United States</ref>
                            </item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg667">Difficulties affecting relations between the
                                    United States and the Soviet Union, and discussions concerning
                                    their alleviation</ref>
                            </item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg768">The beginnings of assistance from the United
                                    States for the Soviet Union after its invasion by Germany</ref>
                            </item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg866">Difficulties from Soviet authorities
                                    interfering with the proper functioning of the American Embassy
                                    in Moscow</ref>
                            </item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg914">Trade relations between the United States and
                                    the Soviet Union; renewal of commercial agreement by exchange of
                                    notes signed August 2, 1941</ref>
                            </item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg926">Arrest and detention of American citizens in
                                    the Soviet Union and of Soviet citizens in the United States,
                                    and arrangements for return to their own countries</ref>
                            </item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg995">Interest of the United States in protection of
                                    church property and in freedom of religious worship in the
                                    Soviet Union</ref>
                            </item>
                            <item>
                                <ref target="#pg1005">Efforts by the United States to persuade the
                                    Soviet Union to adhere to the Geneva Convention of 1929 relative
                                    to the treatment of prisoners of war</ref>
                            </item>
                        </list>
                    </item>
                    <item>
                        <ref target="#pg1027">
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Index</hi>
                        </ref>
                    </item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
